{
 "summary": "Fixed FITS Card round trips so consecutive single quotes survive CONTINUE cards. The writer keeps escaped quote pairs together. The reader joins escaped fragments before decoding once and still accepts older images that split a pair. Quoted slashes in values no longer look like comment delimiters.",
 "changed_files": [
  "astropy/io/fits/card.py",
  "astropy/io/fits/util.py",
  "astropy/io/fits/tests/test_header.py"
 ],
 "verification": "Completed, high confidence. Checked the existing test_long_string_value_via_fromstring owner for permissive parsing and left it intact. Added dedicated round-trip, physical card boundary, and legacy-read coverage beside it. RED: python3 -m pytest astropy/io/fits/tests/test_header.py -q -k 'long_string_quote_roundtrip or long_string_escaped_quote_at_card_boundary or long_string_read_split_escaped_quote' exited 1: five failures showed lost quotes, misread value text, or a split escape; the legacy case passed. GREEN: python3 -m pytest astropy/io/fits/tests/test_header.py -q exited 0, 181 passed. Both original reproduction loops passed all 30 cases. Pre-commit passed for the three changed files. No follow-up refactor.",
 "publication": "Committed as 2406d9a. git push exited 128 because the repository has no configured push destination. No changelog fragment was added because no PR number is available."
}

{
 "summary": "Implemented `solution.py` only. It uses `np.unique(a, return_inverse=True)` for sorted distinct columns and NumPy indexed assignment to fill the integer matrix without a Python loop. It uses the supplied `np` and `a` unchanged.",
 "verification": "The inline `.bench-home/python/bin/python -` harness was the only test seam. RED exited 1 because `solution.py` was absent, after the NumPy inverse-index probe passed. GREEN exited 0 and passed the requested example, duplicate values, and empty input. No refactor was needed. For 100,000 rows and 32 distinct values, the same setup took 4.37 ms with indexed assignment versus 13.37 ms with a Python assignment loop.",
 "publication": "Committed as 522c27e. `git push` exited 128 because no push destination is configured."
}

{
 "summary": "Fixed Moto’s DynamoDB `update_item` numeric `ADD`: Boto3 now reads back `Decimal('11.7')` for `100 + Decimal('-88.3')`. Confidence: high. The ADD executor delegated to `DynamoType.__add__`, where float conversion caused rounding and integer parsing rejected exponent notation. Addition now uses a Decimal context at Boto3’s 38-digit precision rather than Python’s default 28. The shared `SET ... + ...` path uses the same correction; subtraction and legacy updates were left unchanged.",
 "files": [
  "moto/dynamodb/models/dynamo_type.py",
  "tests/test_dynamodb/test_dynamodb_table_with_range_key.py"
 ],
 "verification": "Completed. Baseline: `.bench-home/venv/bin/python -m pytest tests/test_dynamodb/test_dynamodb_table_with_range_key.py` passed 29 tests. Moved the existing numeric ADD assertion into parametrized `test_update_item_add_number_with_expression`, preserving integer coverage. RED: `.bench-home/venv/bin/python -m pytest -q tests/test_dynamodb/test_dynamodb_table_with_range_key.py -k add_number_with_expression` exited 1 (wrong decimal, rejected exponent; integer passed). GREEN: `.bench-home/venv/bin/python -m pytest -q tests/test_dynamodb/test_dynamodb_table_with_range_key.py` exited 0 with 32 passed, without further refactoring. An independent Boto3/Moto probe reproduced both failures before the fix and returned both exact values afterward. `git diff --check` passed. `make lint` was unavailable because `ruff` is not installed. Live AWS was not checked; no AWS credentials were configured.",
 "publication": "Committed as c09ac40. `git push` exited 128 because no remote is configured."
}

